WEBVTT

00:00:04.670 --> 00:00:06.790
Morning starts early at the Demon Queen's castle.

00:00:12.790 --> 00:00:14.630
What a beautiful day.

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:17.080
Perfect weather for a hard day's work.

00:00:19.210 --> 00:00:21.710
As a temp who's gotta prove himself,

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.790
I've gotta get to work before anyone else...

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:34.670
...and take care of what I can to show them
I'm more than motivated!

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.330
Hey, wake up.

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:48.830
Five more minutes...

00:00:49.380 --> 00:00:52.210
The sun's up. Wakey-wakey!

00:00:52.210 --> 00:00:54.880
I get that you're tired, but you've got work to do!

00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:56.500
I'm here to help, so up and at 'em!

00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.290
I don't wanna... I'm just gonna stay in bed.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:03.330
Oh, boy.

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:07.540
Voice Change: Queen Echidna.

00:01:10.130 --> 00:01:10.880
Perfect.

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:15.960
Sorcerer General! Status report
on the new job applicants!

00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:19.790
Surely you don't intend to make your Queen wait!

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.330
I am so terribly sorry, Your Highness!

00:01:22.630 --> 00:01:27.210
We received more applications than expected,
and haven't been able to process them!

00:01:27.210 --> 00:01:29.420
But it's only slightly delayed, I swear!

00:01:29.670 --> 00:01:32.460
So now they're overdue? That's not good.

00:01:32.460 --> 00:01:37.000
Oh, no! I'll step in to ensure
they won't be delayed any further!

00:01:37.250 --> 00:01:42.710
I'll have the list of interview candidates
by tomorrow--no, by the end of today!

00:01:43.040 --> 00:01:44.960
You realize this is why you're not sleeping enough, right?

00:01:44.960 --> 00:01:47.750
No, it's all because I've been lacking in my duties!

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:52.540
Look, you can't do everything by yourself, you know.

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:53.130
Yes, ma'am!

00:01:53.130 --> 00:01:56.040
You should be delegating tasks to people
who work for you, people you trust.

00:01:56.040 --> 00:01:56.790
Yes, ma'am!

00:01:56.790 --> 00:01:58.630
That's part of being a good boss.

00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.380
Yes, ma'am! You are absolutely correct about all--

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:07.710
Morning, Shutina.

00:02:07.710 --> 00:02:09.540
I know it's early, but do you have any work for me?

00:02:14.500 --> 00:02:15.380
Are we under attack?!

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:22.380
Poor Shutina... She must have had a nightmare.

00:02:23.380 --> 00:02:25.080
She must be under so much stress...

00:02:27.040 --> 00:02:30.460
Ikite ikite ikitsukuse

00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:34.920
Hikari o mirai e

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:48.790
Uragirareta kodoku na sekai ni torinokosare

00:02:50.130 --> 00:02:54.330
Miushinatta ashita o osorete ima mo

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:57.460
Ibasho o sagasu

00:02:57.460 --> 00:03:03.960
Hitsuyou to saretai kokoro no sakebi

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:12.750
Karamiau IDENTITY tashikametainda shinjite iikana

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:16.130
Ikite ikite ikitsukuse

00:03:16.130 --> 00:03:20.130
Hikari o mirai e

00:03:20.460 --> 00:03:23.630
Tatoe subete ushinattemo

00:03:23.630 --> 00:03:27.960
Kibou o tsunaide

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:31.670
Boku ga koko ni iru imi

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.540
Ima wa wakaranakute mo ii

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.420
Kimi to waraiaeru you ni

00:03:39.420 --> 00:03:45.330
Jibun de tachikitte susumudake

00:03:56.420 --> 00:04:01.170
<b>Strive to Ease the Burden on Your Future Self!</b>

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:01.130
I can't believe you. Honestly...

00:04:01.540 --> 00:04:06.000
I can NOT believe you! Totally unbelievable!

00:04:03.580 --> 00:04:07.830
Hey, why're you mumbling and
grumbling to yourself over there?

00:04:07.830 --> 00:04:09.540
What's got you so worked up?

00:04:10.500 --> 00:04:12.580
You! Who else?!

00:04:12.880 --> 00:04:16.000
Every! Infinitesimal! Speck!

00:04:16.330 --> 00:04:20.000
Of your existence!

00:04:20.420 --> 00:04:25.080
The Demon Army was suffering
from a dire lack of personnel.

00:04:25.710 --> 00:04:29.670
After my highly-destructive assault on their army,

00:04:30.170 --> 00:04:35.290
most of the top brass had returned to
the Demon World to recover from their injuries.

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:41.630
The work they'd left behind had to be handled
by those who remained: the Four Generals.

00:04:42.290 --> 00:04:47.710
And nobody knew how to do that work--
no one, save for Shutina.

00:04:48.000 --> 00:04:53.080
It's the sort of thing that plagues big companies:
work veterans can handle easily,

00:04:53.500 --> 00:04:58.380
but those veterans don't have time to write
a manual or train other people to do those tasks.

00:04:58.790 --> 00:05:03.880
Then you have Queen Echidna, who wants
to refortify her army as soon as possible.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:06.540
And someone just can't help
but overwork themselves to do it.

00:05:06.830 --> 00:05:09.790
Even if it means overworking herself to death.

00:05:11.250 --> 00:05:15.250
That explains why her Icicle Lance barely packs a punch.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.920
I came here to help with your workload, y'know.

00:05:21.250 --> 00:05:23.710
You could be a little nicer to me.

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.000
Are you insane?!

00:05:25.210 --> 00:05:29.460
Why in the world would I be nice to a man
who barges into my room while I'm sleeping?!

00:05:29.460 --> 00:05:31.460
I mean, you're a succubus, aren't you?

00:05:32.540 --> 00:05:34.500
Don't say that!

00:05:43.380 --> 00:05:45.790
This is your current task list?

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:49.040
Yes, with the highest-priority tasks at the top.

00:05:49.420 --> 00:05:54.170
Evaluate applications, reorganize sorcerer corps,

00:05:54.170 --> 00:06:00.750
regular maintenance on Queen Echidna's
retainer homunculi, operating cost reduction...

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:04.830
There's like, fifty tasks on here.
Why don't you delegate some of them?

00:06:04.830 --> 00:06:08.000
To whom?! I don't have any colleagues or subordinates!

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.380
All right, all right.

00:06:09.960 --> 00:06:11.830
The last task on this list is...

00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:15.040
Replenishing the mana reactors.

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:16.790
What're you looking at?

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:18.380
Let me think here.

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:24.540
A number of castle facilities and instruments
tapped into mana from the reactors.

00:06:25.210 --> 00:06:30.790
Only the person who created them
can replenish them with mana.

00:06:31.460 --> 00:06:36.750
So any reactors that Shutina created could
only be replenished by Shutina herself.

00:06:36.750 --> 00:06:40.960
If anyone with a different mana wavelength tried
to help, the reactor would be destroyed.

00:06:41.960 --> 00:06:43.460
But that's where I come in.

00:06:43.460 --> 00:06:45.210
What's that smirk for?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.170
From today on, I'm gonna handle
replenishing your mana reactors.

00:06:49.420 --> 00:06:53.040
Thank you, that's wonderful.
That task is quite the headache to handle.

00:06:53.830 --> 00:06:55.380
You're not going to ask how I'll do it?

00:06:55.380 --> 00:07:00.130
You're going to mimic my wavelength
with Harmonize, right? It's common sense.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:04.040
It's only common sense to sorcerers
as powerful as we are.

00:07:05.460 --> 00:07:08.080
So, how many reactors are yours?

00:07:08.080 --> 00:07:09.380
Just four.

00:07:09.630 --> 00:07:14.540
Not many, considering there are over
a hundred throughout the castle.

00:07:15.130 --> 00:07:17.750
They only have to be replenished once every few days.

00:07:18.630 --> 00:07:19.670
Got it.

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.710
Give me thirty minutes and two hours.

00:07:22.420 --> 00:07:24.630
Thirty minutes and two hours and I'll have it done.

00:07:25.580 --> 00:07:28.920
I could get it done in less than an hour.

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.170
Don't be like that.

00:07:30.420 --> 00:07:33.080
I'll promise you this, and stake my honor as a Hero on it.

00:07:33.080 --> 00:07:33.960
Promise me what?

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:37.330
I promise to never, ever disappoint you.

00:07:37.420 --> 00:07:39.210
In two and a half hours, you'll be all like,

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:43.170
"Oh yay, my workload is gonna be sooo light!
You're amazing, Leo! I love you so much!"

00:07:43.170 --> 00:07:46.290
Then you'll jump up and give me a huge kiss!

00:07:47.920 --> 00:07:49.210
Fine, go get it done.

00:07:49.540 --> 00:07:51.460
That's all you have to say?

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.500
It's been fourteen seconds.

00:07:53.500 --> 00:07:55.210
All right, I'm going...

00:07:56.500 --> 00:07:57.830
Metamorphose!

00:08:04.330 --> 00:08:07.960
Wait, I gotta think up a name. Something super cool.

00:08:07.960 --> 00:08:09.630
Thirty seconds now.

00:08:09.630 --> 00:08:11.170
Oh, one favor, actually!

00:08:11.580 --> 00:08:16.920
Could you give me the title "Assistant to the Generals"?
That'll get people to trust me.

00:08:17.750 --> 00:08:19.040
Very well.

00:08:19.040 --> 00:08:20.000
Thanks.

00:08:21.710 --> 00:08:24.580
How's the name Godhart sound to you?

00:08:24.580 --> 00:08:25.920
Get a move on already!

00:08:46.500 --> 00:08:48.000
...and that's why I've come to you all.

00:08:48.380 --> 00:08:51.790
If you notice Shutina acting off at all,
let me know immediately.

00:08:51.790 --> 00:08:52.920
Understood.

00:08:54.250 --> 00:08:56.630
I wish I could be of help to her...

00:08:57.000 --> 00:08:59.880
You shouldn't. Shutina would stress out more if you did.

00:09:00.170 --> 00:09:03.830
You're right. Thank you, everyone.

00:09:03.830 --> 00:09:04.540
Of course.

00:09:09.040 --> 00:09:10.420
I'll help!

00:09:10.630 --> 00:09:14.210
Yeah! I got this!

00:09:14.420 --> 00:09:15.790
I can do this!

00:09:19.540 --> 00:09:20.750
I've returned, milady.

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:23.250
Why are you talking like that?

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.170
Milady.

00:09:26.790 --> 00:09:30.670
I figured I'd change up my speaking
style to blend in better.

00:09:32.830 --> 00:09:34.880
It's only been thirty minutes.

00:09:34.880 --> 00:09:37.830
Have a little faith. I took care of it.

00:09:38.170 --> 00:09:41.040
I suppose I should give you another task, then...

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:43.040
No, not yet. I'm kinda tired.

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:43.540
What?

00:09:43.920 --> 00:09:47.210
It's been a while since I've adjusted
my mana wavelength.

00:09:52.290 --> 00:09:53.420
Mirage Eye?

00:09:53.710 --> 00:09:56.880
I want to watch you work while I take a little break.

00:09:59.080 --> 00:10:01.960
I won't get in your way. I'll sit here quietly.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.790
I've got another task for you when
you're done resting, all right?

00:10:18.920 --> 00:10:21.920
Leo, you must be rested by now. I need you to--

00:10:21.920 --> 00:10:24.380
Not yet. I need to rest just a little longer.

00:10:24.630 --> 00:10:27.830
It's been a while since I've used Metamorphose.

00:10:31.170 --> 00:10:32.670
This stuff's pretty bland.

00:10:33.130 --> 00:10:35.630
I should see about improving the food around here, too...

00:10:46.710 --> 00:10:50.420
It's been an hour! Surely you're more than rested!

00:10:50.420 --> 00:10:53.710
No, I need a little more. My mana's still recovering.

00:10:53.710 --> 00:10:54.920
You lazy bastard!

00:10:54.920 --> 00:10:57.040
Get up this instant!

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:00.210
How are you this heavy?!

00:11:01.580 --> 00:11:04.040
Most sorcerers don't realize you can
use Gravity Root to do this!

00:11:04.460 --> 00:11:07.750
You've got enough mana to waste on silly spells,
but you still need to 'recover'?!

00:11:11.130 --> 00:11:15.630
Decisions, decisions... Do I go with
Lord Godhart or Lord Bloodsword?

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:19.750
Wait, I could go with something totally different:
Black Knight Onyx.

00:11:19.750 --> 00:11:21.540
What do you think of that, Shutina?

00:11:22.210 --> 00:11:23.130
What's up?

00:11:23.130 --> 00:11:24.960
I understand full well now, Hero Leo.

00:11:25.670 --> 00:11:31.750
You're a worthless, lazy leech of time and resources!

00:11:31.750 --> 00:11:34.170
Whoa, whoa, calm down!

00:11:34.170 --> 00:11:35.380
I'm calm.

00:11:35.710 --> 00:11:39.080
And after calmly and coolly thinking this over,

00:11:39.080 --> 00:11:44.630
I've come to the calm conclusion that
you will not be of use to our army in the slightest!

00:11:45.170 --> 00:11:47.250
Dio Neel Zod, spiral of radiant light...

00:11:47.250 --> 00:11:48.710
Whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:11:48.710 --> 00:11:51.920
Fill my hands with your piercing rays of the gods!

00:11:51.920 --> 00:11:54.420
Stop! You're going to destroy all your paperwork!

00:11:54.420 --> 00:11:55.920
Gae Assail!

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:01.040
Yes!

00:12:03.380 --> 00:12:05.500
I'm going to join the Demon Queen's legion.

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:08.790
I have to, for good reason.

00:12:09.250 --> 00:12:14.460
And if I want to join, I'll need to show results
and get the Generals on my side.

00:12:15.630 --> 00:12:17.880
This, right here, is step one!

00:12:22.250 --> 00:12:26.380
Dianette, yes? Good work.

00:12:26.380 --> 00:12:29.250
By the look of you, all must have gone well.

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:31.380
Yes, Lord Godhart.

00:12:31.380 --> 00:12:34.170
Please, call me Black Knight Onyx.

00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:37.380
From now on-- no, FORSOOTH? Henceforth?

00:12:37.380 --> 00:12:39.330
Anyway, Black Knight Onyx, understood?

00:12:39.330 --> 00:12:41.210
Y-yes, Lord Onyx...

00:12:41.460 --> 00:12:45.380
Right then, proceed with your report
on the reactor maintenance.

00:12:45.960 --> 00:12:47.170
Yes, milord.

00:12:49.080 --> 00:12:54.210
The talisman you granted me
worked without incident, Lord Onyx.

00:12:54.420 --> 00:12:55.880
It appears to be durable enough to--

00:12:55.880 --> 00:12:57.420
Wait, wait, hold on!

00:12:57.420 --> 00:12:59.670
What talisman? What are you talking about?

00:12:59.920 --> 00:13:03.710
Le-- Lord Onyx, was it not you
who replenished the reactors?

00:13:03.710 --> 00:13:05.540
Oh, uh...

00:13:05.540 --> 00:13:09.170
Please, let her finish her report, Sorcerer General.

00:13:11.000 --> 00:13:12.170
Go on, then.

00:13:12.170 --> 00:13:13.880
Y-yes, milady.

00:13:14.210 --> 00:13:18.290
The talisman appears to be
durable enough for continued use,

00:13:18.290 --> 00:13:24.880
so with your permission, I would like us to continue
replenishing the reactors in your stead.

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:28.130
Would that be allowed, General Shutina?

00:13:28.420 --> 00:13:33.500
But those are reactors that I created.
You'll be able to replenish them?

00:13:33.710 --> 00:13:35.790
I'll take it from here.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:43.380
First, let me explain what exactly I was doing
in those thirty minutes I was gone.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:50.210
I went to the castle workshop and procured
an amethyst from the goblin goldsmith.

00:13:51.000 --> 00:13:54.790
I filled the amethyst with mana tuned to your wavelength.

00:13:55.670 --> 00:14:01.080
Amethysts are sturdy stones.
They'll stay attuned to a wavelength indefinitely.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:05.710
Anyone who holds it on their person
will be attuned to your wavelength as well.

00:14:06.380 --> 00:14:08.210
So I created a talisman with the stone,

00:14:08.710 --> 00:14:10.580
which only took fifteen minutes.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:19.500
I left the workshop, then lost five minutes
to an unexpected distraction.

00:14:19.790 --> 00:14:21.000
Hey, it's Leo!

00:14:23.080 --> 00:14:25.540
Then I took five minutes to find Dianette here.

00:14:26.460 --> 00:14:30.170
With my last five minutes, I showed her how
to use the talisman to replenish the reactors.

00:14:31.380 --> 00:14:37.880
He told me as long as I'm wearing this talisman,
I can replenish all of your reactors.

00:14:37.880 --> 00:14:39.920
After that, I said:

00:14:40.710 --> 00:14:47.000
Find a few other people with the
appropriate ability and split the job up.

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:47.920
Yes, milord.

00:14:48.460 --> 00:14:50.080
I found three other sorcerers of similar capacity.

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:54.880
We passed the talisman around to refill the reactors.

00:14:54.880 --> 00:14:56.040
Excellent.

00:14:56.500 --> 00:14:59.920
I trust, then, that all four of you
understand the procedure?

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.880
The Sorcerer General is a busy woman.

00:15:03.880 --> 00:15:09.250
Form a team of four and assume responsibility
for replenishing her reactors henceforth.

00:15:09.580 --> 00:15:12.830
I'll have enough talismans for all of
you within the next three days.

00:15:12.830 --> 00:15:13.630
Yes, milord!

00:15:14.210 --> 00:15:18.630
You took a bit longer than I'd like for this task,
but it IS your first time.

00:15:19.170 --> 00:15:22.750
I expect you to perform it more quickly come tomorrow.

00:15:23.040 --> 00:15:24.130
Of course, milord!

00:15:24.210 --> 00:15:26.000
That will be all.

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:29.380
Wait, uh, I...

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.460
As you can see, the mana reactors
have been replenished.

00:15:34.170 --> 00:15:37.750
It is our duty to lessen the burden on your shoulders.

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:42.750
Dianette, here, was worried for your health as well.

00:15:43.540 --> 00:15:44.670
She was?

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.630
Oh, m-my apologies, but yes.

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:52.250
I know you've been grappling with a mountain
of tasks in recent days, General Shutina.

00:16:01.880 --> 00:16:04.540
M-might I be of some assistance, General Shutina?

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:12.040
I'm fine. You focus on your own tasks.

00:16:13.920 --> 00:16:18.500
I had neither the courage nor ability to press the matter...

00:16:20.130 --> 00:16:25.460
But thanks to Lord Onyx, we'll be able
to assist with the mana reactors!

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:30.330
If there's anything else we can help with,
please don't hesitate to ask!

00:16:32.130 --> 00:16:34.580
I-I see. Very well.

00:16:35.040 --> 00:16:38.830
I will be sure to reach out to you if there
are tasks you can help with, Dianette.

00:16:38.830 --> 00:16:39.670
Yes, milady!

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:42.460
Good work. You are dismissed.

00:16:42.460 --> 00:16:43.380
Yes, milady!

00:16:45.500 --> 00:16:46.540
Thank you, milady!

00:16:52.630 --> 00:16:57.040
T'would seem you finally understand
my true labors, Sorcerer General.

00:17:00.830 --> 00:17:04.040
All you need to do now is let them handle it
and hear their reports.

00:17:04.380 --> 00:17:07.210
You'll only have to help out if something goes wrong.

00:17:10.380 --> 00:17:13.250
I told you, I only needed two and a half hours,

00:17:13.250 --> 00:17:16.580
and now your workload is permanently decreased.

00:17:18.420 --> 00:17:21.710
Work isn't something that should be done alone.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:25.580
Especially not in a large organization where
there are plenty of people who can help.

00:17:26.130 --> 00:17:29.130
Instead of having one extremely-skilled
person work extremely hard,

00:17:29.130 --> 00:17:32.750
it's best to delegate many
small tasks out to less skilled people.

00:17:33.420 --> 00:17:36.170
That's how you should get most of the work done.

00:17:37.080 --> 00:17:40.040
In an ideal world, of course.

00:17:41.420 --> 00:17:43.500
Why didn't you explain that earlier?

00:17:43.790 --> 00:17:45.960
You could have told me you asked Dianette to help.

00:17:46.210 --> 00:17:48.170
Because you worry too much.

00:17:48.170 --> 00:17:51.710
If I'd told you, you would've rushed off
to "go check on her".

00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:59.880
Most of the people in the army are people you
interviewed, people you trust to perform well.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:04.290
So trust in your judgment,
and in the people working beneath you!

00:18:05.380 --> 00:18:10.080
Run the organization so it could still function
if you dropped dead tomorrow.

00:18:11.830 --> 00:18:14.880
That's a lot of talk for someone
who insisted on working alone.

00:18:15.540 --> 00:18:17.750
I've got a lot of life experience under my belt.

00:18:17.750 --> 00:18:19.170
Wait! Wait just a second!

00:18:19.790 --> 00:18:22.960
You make a big show of 'teaching'
and 'delegating' to a subordinate,

00:18:22.960 --> 00:18:27.580
and while they were hard at work,
you did nothing but loaf about in my office!

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:29.830
You slacker! What's your excuse for that?

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:34.170
You wound me. I was loafing, yes,
but I was also working.

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.000
What?

00:18:35.290 --> 00:18:36.130
Here.

00:18:36.790 --> 00:18:40.420
I learned a lot about from watching you
and your cleavage work.

00:18:40.880 --> 00:18:43.170
I spotted some inefficiencies here and there.

00:18:43.670 --> 00:18:47.170
I took the liberty of rearranging
your priorities. Take a look.

00:18:48.040 --> 00:18:49.250
Let me see.

00:18:54.920 --> 00:18:56.750
Wait, did you say CLEAVAGE?

00:18:57.420 --> 00:18:59.880
See those seven tasks I circled in red?

00:19:00.210 --> 00:19:02.460
You can delegate those.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:06.330
But can they handle it?

00:19:07.000 --> 00:19:10.880
Teach them HOW to handle it.
That's your job as their boss.

00:19:16.040 --> 00:19:17.540
Is this a map of the Largo Sea?

00:19:18.000 --> 00:19:20.170
The fish from that area are fantastic.

00:19:21.130 --> 00:19:24.000
We could make some scrumptious meals
if we got some delivered,

00:19:24.000 --> 00:19:27.330
but considering how dangerous
the shipping route would be...

00:19:27.330 --> 00:19:28.080
Leo.

00:19:30.420 --> 00:19:32.710
Yes, Sorcerer General Shutina?

00:19:33.540 --> 00:19:36.790
I apologize. I've gravely misjudged you.

00:19:36.790 --> 00:19:40.170
C'mon, now. I just did my job is all.

00:19:40.380 --> 00:19:41.960
That only makes it worse.

00:19:42.830 --> 00:19:45.920
Despite how harshly I acted
towards you during the interview,

00:19:46.750 --> 00:19:49.880
you still pressed on and did an excellent job.

00:19:50.250 --> 00:19:54.080
I couldn't well call myself one of the Four Generals
if I didn't thank you for that.

00:19:56.420 --> 00:19:57.790
Don't mention it.

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:02.290
If you go down, the whole army goes down with you.

00:20:02.710 --> 00:20:05.330
And then I REALLY won't have a place to go anymore.

00:20:05.750 --> 00:20:09.290
I was just looking out for myself.
No need to thank me for that.

00:20:09.830 --> 00:20:14.330
And here I was giving you a heartfelt apology!
How is anyone supposed to like you?!

00:20:14.580 --> 00:20:16.670
Why do you think I was traveling alone for so long?

00:20:17.750 --> 00:20:22.130
All right, better start on my next task.
Call me if you need me.

00:20:22.420 --> 00:20:23.670
Before you go...

00:20:24.130 --> 00:20:26.630
I'm looking forward to working with you, Leo.

00:20:33.040 --> 00:20:34.330
Oh, I forgot!

00:20:34.330 --> 00:20:35.500
What is it?

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:38.500
Remember what I said after you gave me this task?

00:20:38.880 --> 00:20:44.040
I promised I wouldn't disappoint you,
then I said something after that.

00:20:44.040 --> 00:20:44.880
Huh?

00:20:45.630 --> 00:20:47.130
In two and a half hours, you'll be all like,

00:20:47.130 --> 00:20:51.250
"Oh yay, my workload is gonna be sooo light!
You're amazing, Leo! I love you so much!"

00:20:51.250 --> 00:20:54.130
Then you'll jump up and give me a huge kiss!

00:20:55.540 --> 00:20:56.920
Fine, go get it done.

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:01.040
I'll take one on the lips, or on the cheek.

00:21:01.500 --> 00:21:03.500
We could even climb into the bed and-

00:21:03.500 --> 00:21:06.380
Get the hell out of here!

00:21:06.380 --> 00:21:08.750
That hurt WAY more than this morning!

00:21:25.710 --> 00:21:26.750
What is it?

00:21:27.130 --> 00:21:29.750
You told me to call you if I needed you, yes?

00:21:31.880 --> 00:21:33.630
I didn't think you'd be calling me so soon.

00:21:34.500 --> 00:21:35.330
You see...

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:37.830
Lily is headed to Largo on a logistics mission.

00:21:38.210 --> 00:21:41.210
The castle's food and equipment stores are running low,

00:21:41.420 --> 00:21:44.540
so we need to make sure this shipment comes in safe.

00:21:45.460 --> 00:21:47.460
Yeah, that could be a serious issue.

00:21:48.880 --> 00:21:50.830
And that's not the only problem.

00:21:53.290 --> 00:21:56.920
Here's the mission plan Lily submitted to me...

00:21:57.880 --> 00:22:00.960
Everyone's gonna have a big happy time!

00:22:04.210 --> 00:22:05.380
For real?

00:22:17.790 --> 00:22:24.040
Bokura no kokoro wa itsudatte moroi

00:22:24.040 --> 00:22:30.210
Sore demo mae o muite nagai michi o susumu

00:22:30.290 --> 00:22:35.880
Shiranakatta koto wa kore kara shireba ii

00:22:36.170 --> 00:22:42.790
Tsuzukeru koto no saki ni aru mono ima wa mada wakaranai kedo

00:22:43.000 --> 00:22:48.830
Hitori de kakaekomi suginaide tama ni wa senaka o azuketemiyou

00:22:49.080 --> 00:22:52.580
Yowasa ni yorisoeru no mo tsuyosanara

00:22:52.580 --> 00:22:57.000
Madamada saki wa nagai kui no nai you ni

00:22:57.500 --> 00:23:00.420
Hashiridase riyuu wa tanjun

00:23:00.420 --> 00:23:03.880
Tokihanate risou no yume o

00:23:03.880 --> 00:23:10.000
Fumidashita saki no mirai wa jibun shidai de dou ni demo naru

00:23:10.000 --> 00:23:15.710
Kawaru koto ga kowakunattemo sukoshizutsu de iinda

00:23:15.710 --> 00:23:19.880
Taisetsu na mono o mamoru tame ni

00:23:19.880 --> 00:23:22.460
Megurimegutte tsunagatta

00:23:22.460 --> 00:23:26.790
Kimi ni arigatou todoiteimasu you ni

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.080
<b>Next Time:</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.080
<b>A Little Bit of</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.080
<b>Thought Goes</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.080
<b>A Long Way</b>

00:23:36.460 --> 00:23:41.080
<b>for Efficiency!</b>
